// stop_channel -- operation model §3.2, group 1, level: end-to-end.
//
// completes_when: STOP written; the channel has aborted, ERR is set, and the
//                 error interrupt (if enabled) has been raised.
// waits for:      channel ERR, on the per-channel interrupt. An abort path
//                 that completes the SAME outstanding request from a second
//                 entry point.
//
// An abort is reported as an ERROR, not as a clean stop -- carried into the
// contract verbatim. Note the consequence for the scenario layer: the aborted
// transfer_single() also returns, with status WB_DMA_ERROR. Two blocking
// operations complete off one event.
//
// THE ONE PLACE TWO OPERATIONS SHARE A CHANNEL. By definition this aborts a
// transfer that is still running, so it violates the one-operation-per-channel
// rule that makes the polling read in wait_completion() safe. Two consequences:
//
//   * The read-modify-write below reads CHn_CSR, which clears ERR and the
//     interrupt sources. That read happens BEFORE STOP is written, so it can
//     only consume status that was already there -- the abort's own ERR is set
//     afterwards and is still seen by the waiting transfer. What it can lose is
//     a completion that landed in the instant before the abort.
//   * Both this call and the aborted transfer_single() then poll the same CSR,
//     and whichever reads first consumes the ERR. Which of the two returns the
//     status and which spins is not determined by this model.
//
// open (§6.5): is write-1-to-STOP acknowledged before or after the current
//              WISHBONE cycle retires? That decides whether this operation can
//              return before the bus is quiet, which matters post-silicon.
import wb_dma_regs_pkg::*;
import wb_dma_types_pkg::*;

extend component wb_dma_ch_ops_c {

    target function wb_dma_status_e stop_channel() {
        wb_dma_ch_csr_s csr;

        csr = regs.csr.read();
        csr.stop = 1;
        regs.csr.write(csr);

        return wait_completion();
    }
}
